[38;5;231m⏺[39m Design, section by section.

  [1mSection 1 — The visitor-ID module[0m

  New file [38;5;153msrc/visitor-id.js[39m, an ES module with two exports.

  [34mexport[39m [34mfunction[39m [33mcreateVisitorIdStore[39m(storage) { [32m/* ... */[39m }
  [34mexport[39m [34mfunction[39m [33mgetVisitorId[39m() { [32m/* default, bound to window.localStorage */[39m }

  [38;5;153mcreateVisitorIdStore(storage)[39m returns an object with a single method, [38;5;153mget()[39m. The storage argument only needs
  [38;5;153mgetItem[39m/[38;5;153msetItem[39m, so a plain object literal satisfies it in tests.

  [1mThe value.[0m A v4 UUID from [38;5;153mcrypto.randomUUID()[39m, which is available in all current browsers over HTTPS and on localhost.
  Stored under the key [38;5;153mvisitorId[39m. I'd keep the key unprefixed and simple since nothing else in the app uses storage; if
  you expect other apps on the same origin, say so and I'll namespace it.

  [1mResolution order on [38;5;153mget()[39m:[0m return the cached in-memory value if one exists; otherwise read storage; if the stored
  value is missing, empty, or not a well-formed UUID, generate a fresh one, persist it, and cache it.

  [1mWhen storage misbehaves.[0m [38;5;153mlocalStorage[39m throws in some private-browsing modes and when quota is exhausted, and a stored
  value can be corrupt. In every one of those cases the module falls back to an in-memory ID that lives for the page's
  lifetime: tracking degrades to per-page instead of the whole feature throwing inside a login handler. [38;5;153mget()[39m never
  throws and never returns null — that's the invariant the tests pin down.

  [1mDeliberately excluded:[0m no ID rotation, no expiry, no cross-tab synchronization, no consent gating. Say the word if any
  of those are actually required, since consent in particular would change the design rather than extend it.

  Does this section look right before I move to how [38;5;153mlogin()[39m and the page wire into it?

